  id: Left_Artium
  partName: Left Artium
  descriptionChunks:
  - The atria are the upper chambers of the heart that receive blood returning to
    the heart. The left atrium receives oxygenated blood from the lungs. These chambers
    play a key role in regulating blood flow into the ventricles.
  - By ensuring proper filling of the heart, they contribute to efficient circulation.
    Their coordinated function is essential for maintaining a steady and continuous
    flow of blood throughout the body.
